    "body": "Uhm, should is not non-normative. See also https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#conformance. A \"should\" is a requirement that you can chose not to follow if you have a very good reason for not following that requirement. It's still a normative requirement and can be tested. And if everyone plans to implement it perhaps we ought to make it a \"must\" instead.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
